  "steps": [
    "Soak 1 cup black chickpeas overnight then pressure cook for 4-5 whistles until soft.",
    "For the coconut masala: Take 1 small cup of grated fresh coconut and roast it until it turns a little brown. In a kadhai, roast 2-3 tbsp peanuts, curry leaves, 2 dried red chillies. Then add roasted coconut, 1 tsp red chilli powder, salt, 1 tsp dhaniya powder, 1/2 tsp haldi, 1/4 tsp cinnamon powder, 1 tsp garam masala. Roast for a min and take it off the flame.",
    "Add some ghee in a kadhai. Then add 1/2 tsp fennel seeds (saunf), 5-6 cloves of chopped garlic, 3-4 chopped chillies, chopped ginger. Then add 1 chopped onion and sauté well. After a few minutes add salt, red chilli powder and garam masala. Now add the coconut masala we roasted and let it cook for 2-3 minutes. Then add purée of 2 tomatoes. Let this cook well until soft and mushy and blend into a fine paste.",
    "Now in a pan, add 1 tsp mustard seeds, curry leaves, pinch of hing, 3-4 tbsp onions and the curry we prepared. Let it cook for 2 mins and add boiled chickpeas along with some mashed chickpeas.",
    "Give it a mix and cover and cook for 7-8 mins. Add water to adjust consistency.",
    "Add 1 tbsp of jaggery powder and adjust the masalas as per your taste.",
    "Cook for 5 more minutes and it’s ready. Serve with hot fluffy appams."
  ],
